; Tutorial_7_Convert_Between_Formats.inix -- one file made into another kind.

[about]
Title=7 - Convert Between Formats
Intro=One want: a Word document as a web page, or a PDF as plain text, without opening either. Shift plus O, O for Output, offers what the file can become and converts the tagged files, or the current one, keeping each name.
Setup=A folder holds a Word document and a PDF.
Homework=Convert a Markdown file of your own to a web page, then open the web page in your browser.


[step]

Say=One want: a document in another form -- a Word file as a web page, a PDF as plain text -- without opening it in anything.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus F opens FileDir on the folder it last showed.
Key=Alt+Control+F
Hear=FileDir

[step]

Say=I arrow to a Word document. Shift plus O is Output Type, O for Output.
Key=Shift+O
Hear=Output Type dialog
Hear=Web page
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=FileDir looked at what the file is and offers only what it can become: for a document, Word, a web page, Markdown, plain text, EPUB and others. Down Arrow moves through them.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Markdown
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I want the web page. Up Arrow back to it, then Enter.
Key=Up Arrow
Hear=Web page
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter converts.
Key=Enter
Hear=Converted to report dot h t m l
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The new file lands beside the old one with the same root name, and nothing is ever overwritten. A planned misstep: a PDF offers fewer choices, because only its text can be read out of it. I arrow to one and press Shift plus O.
Key=Shift+O
Hear=Output Type dialog
Hear=Plain text
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Plain text or a web page, and no more: a PDF is a printed page, read back. Escape leaves it as it is.
Key=Escape
Hear=FileDir
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Tagged files convert together: tag several, then Shift plus O once. What this walk taught. I name the step; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Choose what this file becomes.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus O

[step]

Say=Leave without converting.
Key=
Hear=Escape
